# Terminal flood / Follow: run the app

`cargo test` and a green compile do **not** prove flood is smooth. Ingest can
busy-loop the event loop at 100% CPU while tests still pass. A **debug** binary
also pegs ~100% of a core on the same flood even when `release-dev` sits ~25% —
measuring the wrong binary is how false “fixed” reports happen.

Linux and Windows use the **same acceptance**. Pick the command column for the
**current host**.

## Acceptance (both hosts)

After **any** change to PTY ingest, HOST_TICK, Follow, WRAP, Viewport paint,
or live Terminal rendering:

1. Do **not** tell the user to rebuild or "try the flood again".
2. Kill leftover `noviewlog-slint` processes (stale process = stale 100% CPU).
3. Build/run the daily **`release-dev`** binary — never `target/debug/`.
4. Visible window, Follow **on**, WRAP **on** and WRAP **off**.
5. **Fail** if that PID pegs ~100% of a core, the tail teleports, WRAP-on Follow
   is unusable, or the status line sticks at `max_scrollback` (~10000/10000) and
   “pages” every ring trim. Follow must look like a native terminal (monotonic
   line total, live screen). `cargo test` passing is not acceptance.
6. If there is no display session, say so and do **not** claim the hitch is fixed.

## Host commands

| Step | Linux | Windows |
|------|-------|---------|
| Kill leftovers | stop leftover `noviewlog-slint` PIDs | `Get-Process noviewlog-slint -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue \| Stop-Process` |
| Daily run | `bash scripts/run-slint.sh` (must be `cargo run --profile release-dev`) | `.\scripts\run-slint-windows.ps1` (MSVC env required / imported by the script) |
| Prove binary | `readlink -f /proc/<pid>/exe` contains `target/release-dev/` — **fail** if `target/debug/` | `(Get-Process noviewlog-slint).Path` contains `target\release-dev\` — **fail** if `target\debug\` |
| Flood | `cat` a large access-log style file (long URLs) in the in-app terminal | `type big.log` or `Get-Content big.log` in the in-app terminal |
| Sample CPU | `pidstat` / `top` for that PID for several seconds | `Get-Process noviewlog-slint \| Select-Object Id, CPU, Path` twice with `Start-Sleep` between samples |
| Report | PID, `%CPU`, `/proc/<pid>/exe` | PID, CPU trend, `.Path` |
